  "result": "CommonJS module with order helpers: sum line totals, apply a percentage discount code, average item price, and render an order as text.\n\nBugs:\n1. `orders.js:5` — off-by-one: `i <= items.length` reads `items[length]` (undefined) → TypeError on every call.\n2. `orders.js:20` — `averageItemPrice([])` returns `NaN` (0/0); no empty-array guard.\n3. `orders.js:13` — `discounts[code]` hits the prototype chain: codes like `\"constructor\"` or `\"toString\"` return a function, so `pct === undefined` is false and `total - total*fn/100` → `NaN`. Use `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(discounts, code)` (or a `Map`/`null`-prototype object).\n4. `orders.js:26` — `formatOrder` on an empty `items` array yields a leading `\"\\n\"` before `Total:`.",
